<item>
<title>Yap on Cairn: the overlay</title>
<link>https://cairn.iamnbutler.workers.dev/milestones/#yap-on-cairn-the-overlay</link>
<guid isPermaLink="false">https://cairn.iamnbutler.workers.dev/m/videos/796054c4982eb3e6.mp4</guid>
<pubDate>Sat, 24 Oct 2026 07:16:39 GMT</pubDate>
<description>&lt;figure&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cairn.iamnbutler.workers.dev/m/videos/796054c4982eb3e6.mp4&quot;&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://cairn.iamnbutler.workers.dev/m/videos/796054c4982eb3e6.jpg&quot; width=&quot;1112&quot; height=&quot;428&quot; alt=&quot;Yap on Cairn: the overlay&quot;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;figcaption&gt;Yap's dictation overlay on Cairn, driven by a synthetic voice: recording with a moving tape waveform and a two-line live preview, then transcribing, then typed. The state, view and layout are Lean; the waveform is a host-drawn paint node running the original's Metal shader.&lt;/figcaption&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cairn.iamnbutler.workers.dev/m/videos/796054c4982eb3e6.mp4&quot;&gt;Watch the video&lt;/a&gt; (11 s), recorded at commit a83d447, in the progress log of &lt;a href=&quot;https://cairn.iamnbutler.workers.dev/milestones/#second-milestone-yap-on-cairn&quot;&gt;Second milestone: Yap on Cairn&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
</item>
<item>
<title>Second milestone: Yap on Cairn</title>
<link>https://cairn.iamnbutler.workers.dev/milestones/#second-milestone-yap-on-cairn</link>
<guid isPermaLink="true">https://cairn.iamnbutler.workers.dev/milestones/#second-milestone-yap-on-cairn</guid>
<pubDate>Sat, 24 Oct 2026 01:04:46 GMT</pubDate>
<description>&lt;p&gt;Can claims hold up on real software someone uses every day? Yap is a small dictation app for
    the Mac: hold a key, talk, and the transcript is typed into the app in front. Almost all of it
    lives outside its window, so Cairn has to learn the outside world first.&lt;/p&gt;
  &lt;ol&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;Effects: the clock and timers, requests the host performs and answers, and outside inputs
      like a global key and the microphone. Each one is a recorded assumption, fuzzed.&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;New surfaces: a native menu bar menu built from Lean, and an overlay that never takes focus.&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;Proofs about dictation: a shortcut never sends, a transcript is saved before it is typed,
      a late reply never types, every recording ends.&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;Yap rebuilt on Cairn, signed and installed, and used for a real day of work.&lt;/li&gt;
  &lt;/ol&gt;
  &lt;p&gt;Progress so far:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cairn.iamnbutler.workers.dev/milestones/#yap-on-cairn-the-overlay&quot;&gt;Yap on Cairn: the overlay&lt;/a&gt; (2026-10-24)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cairn.iamnbutler.workers.dev/milestones/#clock-effects&quot;&gt;Clock: effects&lt;/a&gt; (2026-10-23)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;</description>
</item>
<item>
<title>Clock: effects</title>
<link>https://cairn.iamnbutler.workers.dev/milestones/#clock-effects</link>
<guid isPermaLink="false">https://cairn.iamnbutler.workers.dev/m/videos/a79d52b1bab3288e.mp4</guid>
<pubDate>Fri, 23 Oct 2026 21:55:36 GMT</pubDate>
<description>&lt;figure&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cairn.iamnbutler.workers.dev/m/videos/a79d52b1bab3288e.mp4&quot;&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://cairn.iamnbutler.workers.dev/m/videos/a79d52b1bab3288e.jpg&quot; width=&quot;960&quot; height=&quot;1104&quot; alt=&quot;Clock: effects&quot;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;figcaption&gt;Cairn's first effects. A stopwatch whose time, ticks, sounds and lap file come from the host as replies to requests Lean makes: Lap plays a sound, Save writes the laps to a file, Reset clears them and Load reads them back. Timers fire within 1–2 ms; a click → read file → frame round trip is 1.5 ms (p50).&lt;/figcaption&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cairn.iamnbutler.workers.dev/m/videos/a79d52b1bab3288e.mp4&quot;&gt;Watch the video&lt;/a&gt; (16 s), recorded at commit 4fc3970, in the progress log of &lt;a href=&quot;https://cairn.iamnbutler.workers.dev/milestones/#second-milestone-yap-on-cairn&quot;&gt;Second milestone: Yap on Cairn&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
</item>
<item>
<title>TodoMVC in Lean</title>
<link>https://cairn.iamnbutler.workers.dev/milestones/#todomvc-in-lean</link>
<guid isPermaLink="false">https://cairn.iamnbutler.workers.dev/m/videos/5cf436dca2cd5034.mp4</guid>
<pubDate>Fri, 23 Oct 2026 17:16:53 GMT</pubDate>
<description>&lt;figure&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cairn.iamnbutler.workers.dev/m/videos/5cf436dca2cd5034.mp4&quot;&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://cairn.iamnbutler.workers.dev/m/videos/5cf436dca2cd5034.jpg&quot; width=&quot;1120&quot; height=&quot;840&quot; alt=&quot;TodoMVC in Lean&quot;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;figcaption&gt;The full TodoMVC, written in Lean and running natively on the Mac. Add, complete, double-click to edit, filter, clear completed, and toggle all. Every control is a claim (^202 to ^211). On the real app, 999 of 1,000 generated conformance sequences matched the Lean model. The one miss is a known edge case: a click that ends an edit can be dropped, as in a browser.&lt;/figcaption&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cairn.iamnbutler.workers.dev/m/videos/5cf436dca2cd5034.mp4&quot;&gt;Watch the video&lt;/a&gt; (28 s), recorded at commit 9224599, in the progress log of &lt;a href=&quot;https://cairn.iamnbutler.workers.dev/milestones/#first-milestone-a-proved-todomvc&quot;&gt;First milestone: a proved TodoMVC&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
</item>
<item>
<title>Basics: the first Lean app</title>
<link>https://cairn.iamnbutler.workers.dev/milestones/#basics-the-first-lean-app</link>
<guid isPermaLink="false">https://cairn.iamnbutler.workers.dev/m/videos/c8a7c8d6ab57ac2f.mp4</guid>
<pubDate>Fri, 23 Oct 2026 15:57:47 GMT</pubDate>
<description>&lt;figure&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cairn.iamnbutler.workers.dev/m/videos/c8a7c8d6ab57ac2f.mp4&quot;&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://cairn.iamnbutler.workers.dev/m/videos/c8a7c8d6ab57ac2f.jpg&quot; width=&quot;960&quot; height=&quot;1264&quot; alt=&quot;Basics: the first Lean app&quot;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;figcaption&gt;A whole app written in Lean: adding, ticking and deleting items. Lean decides the layout, focus, text editing and hit testing; Swift only draws. Every control is a claim (^101 to ^104). Lean proves that an item's Delete button exists exactly when the item does, and that the 'items left' count is right.&lt;/figcaption&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cairn.iamnbutler.workers.dev/m/videos/c8a7c8d6ab57ac2f.mp4&quot;&gt;Watch the video&lt;/a&gt; (17 s), recorded at commit 733224a, in the progress log of &lt;a href=&quot;https://cairn.iamnbutler.workers.dev/milestones/#first-milestone-a-proved-todomvc&quot;&gt;First milestone: a proved TodoMVC&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
</item>
<item>
<title>The host, with text</title>
<link>https://cairn.iamnbutler.workers.dev/milestones/#the-host-with-text</link>
<guid isPermaLink="false">https://cairn.iamnbutler.workers.dev/m/videos/9cb67df1092eb561.mp4</guid>
<pubDate>Fri, 23 Oct 2026 15:18:26 GMT</pubDate>
<description>&lt;figure&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cairn.iamnbutler.workers.dev/m/videos/9cb67df1092eb561.mp4&quot;&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://cairn.iamnbutler.workers.dev/m/videos/9cb67df1092eb561.jpg&quot; width=&quot;1040&quot; height=&quot;904&quot; alt=&quot;The host, with text&quot;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;figcaption&gt;The new AppKit host painting through the Metal renderer: Core Text glyphs from an atlas, a caret, a focused field, a checkbox and a list. Typing goes through the Mac's text-input path, and every control in the accessibility tree is named by its claim id (^1 field, ^2 checkbox, ^3 Add, ^4#1 the new item). This app is the host's test fixture, with its frames built in Swift; the next video is the same host running a Lean app.&lt;/figcaption&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cairn.iamnbutler.workers.dev/m/videos/9cb67df1092eb561.mp4&quot;&gt;Watch the video&lt;/a&gt; (18 s), recorded at commit 3ff02ad, in the progress log of &lt;a href=&quot;https://cairn.iamnbutler.workers.dev/milestones/#first-milestone-a-proved-todomvc&quot;&gt;First milestone: a proved TodoMVC&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
</item>
<item>
<title>Boundary spike</title>
<link>https://cairn.iamnbutler.workers.dev/milestones/#boundary-spike</link>
<guid isPermaLink="false">https://cairn.iamnbutler.workers.dev/m/videos/4dff72519883d7d3.mp4</guid>
<pubDate>Fri, 23 Oct 2026 14:57:34 GMT</pubDate>
<description>&lt;figure&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cairn.iamnbutler.workers.dev/m/videos/4dff72519883d7d3.mp4&quot;&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://cairn.iamnbutler.workers.dev/m/videos/4dff72519883d7d3.jpg&quot; width=&quot;960&quot; height=&quot;704&quot; alt=&quot;Boundary spike&quot;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;figcaption&gt;The first thing on screen. Lean owns the state, the layout and the hit test; Swift forwards clicks and paints Lean's rectangles with Metal. The bar is the count (no text rendering yet). Reset (red) exists only while the count is above zero, which is proved in Lean, and here it's pressed through the accessibility tree.&lt;/figcaption&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cairn.iamnbutler.workers.dev/m/videos/4dff72519883d7d3.mp4&quot;&gt;Watch the video&lt;/a&gt; (9 s), recorded at commit a6b45bc, in the progress log of &lt;a href=&quot;https://cairn.iamnbutler.workers.dev/milestones/#first-milestone-a-proved-todomvc&quot;&gt;First milestone: a proved TodoMVC&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
</item>
<item>
<title>First milestone: a proved TodoMVC</title>
<link>https://cairn.iamnbutler.workers.dev/milestones/#first-milestone-a-proved-todomvc</link>
<guid isPermaLink="true">https://cairn.iamnbutler.workers.dev/milestones/#first-milestone-a-proved-todomvc</guid>
<pubDate>Fri, 23 Oct 2026 14:57:34 GMT</pubDate>
<description>&lt;ol&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;The full TodoMVC app on the Mac, including real text fields and input methods.&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;Every action is a claim with an id that the build refuses to let drift.&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;Proofs: each action does what it says, the counts and filters stay right, and every
      control is present exactly when it should be and can actually be pressed.&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;The real app is driven through a thousand generated sequences and must agree with the model.&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;A map of the app, generated from the claims, showing the evidence behind each one.&lt;/li&gt;
  &lt;/ol&gt;
  &lt;p&gt;Progress so far:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cairn.iamnbutler.workers.dev/milestones/#todomvc-in-lean&quot;&gt;TodoMVC in Lean&lt;/a&gt; (2026-10-23)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cairn.iamnbutler.workers.dev/milestones/#basics-the-first-lean-app&quot;&gt;Basics: the first Lean app&lt;/a&gt; (2026-10-23)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cairn.iamnbutler.workers.dev/milestones/#the-host-with-text&quot;&gt;The host, with text&lt;/a&gt; (2026-10-23)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cairn.iamnbutler.workers.dev/milestones/#boundary-spike&quot;&gt;Boundary spike&lt;/a&gt; (2026-10-23)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;</description>
</item>
